**MPSCALC-134** (Backlog, 0 comments, updated 2026-10-14T02:19). Summary: "e2e helper pdfText() pipes the PDF to pdftotext through a synchronous execFileSync, which can hang a Playwright ..." Quoted: "the first head-live run of proposal-buttons.spec.ts hung 40 minutes after test 12, the worker idle on a child 'pdftotext -layout - -'. execFileSync blocks the worker's event loop, so Playwright's test timeout could not fire. The rerun passed twice (17 s). Not reproduced." and "Fix shape: give execFileSync a timeout (and killSignal) so a stuck child fails the test, or write the PDF to a temp file and use the async execFile with a timeout." and "Regression test the owner should add: with a stand-in pdftotext that never exits, the test fails by its timeout instead of hanging the worker." **No "Done when" line** (count 0, same control). The ticket names ONE file (`proposal-buttons.spec.ts:130`, now `:135`); **main has FOUR call sites** (below). The done-when this kit uses, confirmed by Tuesday in S10: **M2 is done when every `execFileSync('pdftotext', ...)` call in `web/e2e/*.spec.ts` carries a `timeout` and a `killSignal`, a never-exiting stand-in is measured to fail by the timeout (not hang) with the options each edited spec actually holds, and a committed row turns red when any one call loses either option or a new unbounded call appears.** The first fix shape (timeout and killSignal) is the one used; the async-`execFile`-with-temp-file shape is a refactor of four helpers and is NOT used.

