## WHAT TO BUILD (property first; the plants are the proof)
**General property (binding):** *two commits, one per ticket; every expected value a hand-written literal or a value derived by hand from the fixture (never copied from a run's output); every new result green at its branch head and red under its named plant or red on today's code, and green under the other plants; no added test name, comment or message holds a person's name, a decision-card id, a `B###`, a plant id (`P-`, `PC`, `P0`) or a ticket key (the ticket key may appear in the commit SUBJECT only); added lines are ASCII; NO new user-facing word (M1 adds no string literal to `ProposalPage.tsx` at all); no existing result removed or weakened.*

### M1: ignore printAs while a print is pending (MPSCALC-108), `ProposalPage.tsx` and `ProposalPage.test.tsx`
**Property of the product edit:** the only changed lines of `ProposalPage.tsx` are inside `printAs` (`:218`-`:235`) plus ONE new `useRef(false)` declaration beside `page` (`:212`); no import added (`useRef` is imported at `:3`), no string, no JSX, no export, no dependency array other than the existing `[]`. The flag: set at the top of `printAs` BEFORE `flushSync` (an ignored call must not change the format or touch the DOM), after a check that returns at once if it is set; **cleared on every way a print ends**: (a) the synchronous path (`window.print()` at `:225`) in a `try` / `finally`; (b) the image-wait path: the cleared-in-`finally` of the promise chain after `window.print()` has returned or thrown (a `.finally(...)` on the chain, or `async` with `try/finally`); the race always settles (the cap at `:233` is a timer that always fires within `PRINT_IMAGE_WAIT_MS`), so the wait cannot hold the flag forever; (c) it is a `useRef` (not state: no re-render, no stale closure in the `useCallback` with `[]`), so it dies with the component and a remount starts clear. **It must NOT depend on `afterprint` to clear**: `ProposalPage.test.tsx:132` records that some browsers never fire `afterprint`, and a flag cleared only there would stay set for the rest of the page's life: the "stuck flag" this kit exists to prevent. **A stuck flag that blocks every later print is WORSE than the bug it fixes**; the rows that prove the buttons work again are named below, and the plant P-A2 proves they can fail. **Any other shape: prove it meets the property or STOP.**
**What the edit changes for a person (state it in STATUS and in the commit body, in your own words, with counts only):** two presses of either print button inside the image wait (up to `PRINT_IMAGE_WAIT_MS`, 3000 ms; usually the logo's load, about 1.4 s in the gate's measurement) now give ONE dialog; a press of the OTHER button inside that window does nothing (the ticket's fix shape says "ignore printAs while a print is pending"; Q-3 of the drafter's report asks whether that is wanted: default yes); a press after the dialog has opened works as before. **Out of scope and unchanged: on the synchronous path (no pending image) a browser that queues a second click while its blocking print dialog is open delivers it after the dialog closes; that click prints again, as today; the ticket's scenario is the loading logo and nothing here claims more.** Say that in STATUS.
**New rows in `ProposalPage.test.tsx` (inside `describe('Proposal page: the two print buttons (brief B79)'` after the `:159` cap row; none of the existing rows edited; use `spyPrint(false)` and `purchase()`; each expected value hand-written):**
- **D-1 the ticket's regression:** `spyPrint(false)`, `purchase()`, `await screen.findByRole('article', { name: 'Proposal document' })`, `fireEvent.click(shortBtn())` TWICE (a double-click), then load every pending image of `article[aria-label="Short-form proposal"] img` (the existing row `:146`-`:147` shows how: `dispatchEvent(new Event('load'))` inside `await act(async ...)`), then `expect(spy).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)`. Red on today's code with `Expected 1, Received 2` (DERIVED: you print it).
- **D-2 the other button is ignored too, and the document stays the one being printed:** click `shortBtn()`, click `fullBtn()` while the logo is held, load the logo; `expect(spy).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)` and `expect(seen).toEqual([{ full: false, short: true, rental: false }])` (the short form was in the DOM when print opened; the ignored click did not swap the document). Red on today's code (two calls).
- **D-3 the cap path:** fake timers as the `:159` row does; double-click `shortBtn()`; advance `PRINT_IMAGE_WAIT_MS`; `expect(spy).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)`.
- **D-4 THE ROW THAT PROVES THE BUTTON WORKS AGAIN, after the image-wait path:** after D-1's single print, click `fullBtn()` (its images "still loading"), settle its images (as `:150`-`:156`), `expect(spy).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2)`. (The existing `:140` row does the same without a prior double-click; D-4 keeps the proof inside the new group so a later edit of `:140` cannot remove it.)
