**The behaviour probe (Step 6; not committed; in `.tools/b1334/scratch`, stand-ins in `/private/tmp/b1334-seat-tmp`):** a Node script that, for each of the four EDITED specs, takes the options-object text of its `execFileSync('pdftotext'` call BY PROGRAM (the text between the call's third-argument braces), evaluates it as an object literal with `input` replaced by a small buffer, and runs `execFileSync('pdftotext', ['-layout','-','-'], opts)` with `env.PATH` set to the stand-in directory first. The stand-in is `#!/bin/sh` then `exec sleep 600`, `chmod +x`, in `/private/tmp/b1334-seat-tmp` (outside any git tree; `git -C /private/tmp rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree` fails). **Pass predicate: each of the four throws with `code ETIMEDOUT` within `timeout + 3000` ms, measured by `Date.now()`; and the SAME script run over the four S2 blobs (the pre-image, from `git show S2:web/e2e/<name>`) with an outer `timeout 8` has not returned when the outer timeout kills it (the red-first proof: it hangs today). To keep the probe cheap, run it with the options' `timeout` value replaced by 2000 for the timing check ONLY IF the program also prints the unreplaced value read from each spec and asserts it equals `30_000`; otherwise wait the real 30 s per spec (four runs, two minutes).** After every run `ps -axo pid,etime,command` shows no `sleep 600` of yours (control: the pre-image run leaves none because the stand-in `exec`s and the outer `timeout` kills the child; if one is left, kill it by its pid and say so). This probe is the "regression without a heavy full e2e run": no browser, no web, no API, no port.
